# What stays out of the packaged .vsix.
#
# Everything in this folder ships otherwise, and a .vsix is downloaded by every person who
# installs the extension - so what is in it should be what the extension needs to run and
# nothing else.
#
# node_modules is deliberately not listed. vsce works out which packages are production
# dependencies and ships only those, so vscode-languageclient goes in and the TextMate engine
# the tests use does not. Excluding the folder outright would take the language client with it,
# and the server would fail to start on every machine but this one.

# The helpers the test project drives. Nothing extension.js requires reaches them.
tools/**

# Resolved by whoever installs, not carried.
package-lock.json

# The mark itself, which everything showing it reads. The Marketplace wants a PNG and gets one;
# somebody installing the extension has no use for the drawing it was made from.
icon.svg
